{"arguments":{"clientRequestId":"1360be49-6d09-42da-a46f-cdc49e5ecc19","prompt":"Build a complete Inventory Counts app in Arrusted using its current shared CUE/PostgreSQL backend, authenticated context and runtime lifecycle. Builder must author the schema, backend, UI and tests through this public conversation and open a draft PR after validation and publication approval.\n\nReaders can browse active items and paginated count history. Operators can add an item with a unique SKU, name and unit, and submit a nonnegative integer count for that item. A count submission is an immutable audited event with the authenticated operator, server timestamp and a retry key; repeated submission with that key must return the same result. Never trust actor, role, organization or database scope from browser fields. Independent concurrent submissions must both be retained. Use real persistent data with no synthetic product demo or reset control. Retain pilot history indefinitely; item archival must preserve its history.\n\nPrepare your own isolated database and real authenticated identities, including readers, operators and a second tenant. Supply a working authenticated Preview. Exercise browser write/readback after reload, application restart and a new native Preview deployment. Test reader denial of writes, assignment and session revocation, tenant isolation, forged input rejection, replay, concurrency and complete paginated audit history. Author a populated predecessor release and prove an upgrade preserves records and history; prove a failed upgrade leaves the predecessor usable. Verify selected-release packaging and exact-head CI. Keep public transcript, release identity, environment evidence and PR provenance.\n\nUse native Git delivery, Arrusted root Vercel Services and authenticated Gateway. Ask ordinary product questions or visible effect approvals when needed. Production activation is outside this request. Report every acceptance result as passed, failed, blocked or unasses